00:17:57.176 --> 00:17:59.845
A human caught on fire
 will pass out in a matter of seconds

00:17:59.945 --> 00:18:03.148
as the brain slowly shuts off,
 leading to a painful death.

00:18:03.482 --> 00:18:07.519
Also, it looks like a pretty big drop
 to maximize her chances of survival.

00:18:07.619 --> 00:18:10.189
She'll need to cross her legs
 and hit the water feet first.

00:18:10.322 --> 00:18:12.491
She might break her legs,
 but at least she'll survive.

00:18:13.158 --> 00:18:15.694
Maybe diving headfirst
 into a drop like that

00:18:15.694 --> 00:18:19.731
will result in a ninety nine point
 nine percent chance of death jumping feet.

00:18:19.731 --> 00:18:22.868
First is typically how the military
 is trained to jump into water

00:18:22.868 --> 00:18:26.238
off of high platforms,
 such as off of an aircraft carrier.

00:18:26.271 --> 00:18:28.006
When it's time to abandon ship. 

00:18:28.006 --> 00:18:31.944
Now, as far as we know, spontaneous
 human combustion is a concept

00:18:32.077 --> 00:18:35.881
that has arguably zero
 recorded cases in human history.

00:18:35.881 --> 00:18:37.149
So unfortunately for us, 

00:18:37.149 --> 00:18:41.086
it seems like the king might be able
 to defy the laws of chemistry and reality.

00:18:41.386 --> 00:18:43.856
Either way, we have to try what we can.

00:18:44.189 --> 00:18:46.992
If we make it into the water,
 we'll have a good chance of surviving.

00:18:47.126 --> 00:18:49.161
Unless it's Greek fire, then we're doomed.

00:18:49.428 --> 00:18:51.697
It didn't work out for me
 last night. I tried. 

00:18:51.697 --> 00:18:53.132
There have never been cases of people 

00:18:53.132 --> 00:18:56.301
